# Package llm declares no Model with a finite value: its one builder,
# NewMetered, takes a Model, and Retry's Schedule has no generator. So
# llm.Model's laws for Retry, Fallback and Metered run under the named
# contexts of llm/memory (lawRetried, lawFallenBack, lawMetered,
# lawStacked: memory/contexts.ergo), over a script, and llm/recorded runs
# them for Record (lawRecording). Here they are skips.
skip law Model.StreamFoldsToGenerate for Retry: its values have no generator: schedule.spaced has an unexported field, so only package schedule builds it; no exported function of package schedule returns it; bind one in a named context of a test file, let Name = context { Model: … }, and the law runs under it
skip law Model.StreamFoldsToGenerate for Fallback: its values have no generator: Model has no finite value: its builder NewMetered takes an argument that has none, as a builder that needs its own type does; bind one in a named context of a test file, let Name = context { Model: … }, and the law runs under it
